// t_80dad2dd: a PARTIALLY written half colour output.
//
// The reference writes the output register twice and keeps no temp at all -
// `MOVH o[COLH].w, {1}.---x` then `MOVH o[COLH].xyz, f[TEX0].xyz`.  The
// general path instead composes the value in a temp and pins that temp to the
// output slot, which for a half output is H0 - the low half of R0, the very
// register the pin holds.  It therefore REFUSES, by design and by name.
//
// This fixture exists to keep that refusal honest.  It is not a wish for the
// refusal to stay: the day the composition learns to write H0 directly (or
// the allocator learns the output is half before it places anything), this
// test turns red and whoever lifts the refusal inherits a failing test that
// names the shape, rather than a silent H0-vs-R0 mix.  See t_cde25bad.
void main(float4 t : TEXCOORD0, out half4 o : COLOR)
{
    o.xyz = t.xyz;
    o.w = 1.0;
}
